NAME
       kill - send a signal to a process

SYNOPSIS
       kill [-l] [-s sig | -SIG] pid ...

DESCRIPTION
       Sends a signal to each PID. The default is TERM.

OPTIONS
       -l       list the known signal names
       -s SIG   send SIG, given by name or number
       -SIG     the same, written as -9 or -KILL

EXAMPLES
       kill 42
       kill -9 42
       kill -s INT 42

SEE ALSO
       killall(1), ps(1), signals in sigtest(1)
